Article 41, Regional Governments may partner with the business sector, NGOs/social organizations concerned with women and children in the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
The partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out through: (2)
a. provision of information on employment opportunities for women victims of acts of violence;
b. education and training for women and children victims of acts of violence;
c. educational assistance for women and children victims of acts of violence who have been withdrawn from their education; d. fostering and increasing the economic independence of women victims of acts of violence;
e. providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities, private parties and various non-governmental organizations concerned with women and children from various forms of violence; and/or
g. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from various forms of violence up to the Village level.
The partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be set forth in the form of an agreement in accordance with (3) the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 23
Prevention as referred to in Article 22 letter a, is implemented by way of: (1)
a. forming a working network in efforts to prevent violence against women and children;
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns; c. establishing a system for preventing violence against women and children;
d. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence;
e. providing knowledge about prevention and mechanisms for handling violence against women and children; and f. enhancing the role and value of local wisdom as well as the role of customs in the protection of women and children. Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented in an integrated manner by Regional Apparatus whose (2) principal duties and functions are in the fields of: women's empowerment and child protection; education;
health;
social affairs and manpower;
youth and sports; and
f. mental and spiritual.
Regional Apparatus in conducting prevention of acts of (3) violence against women and children as referred to in paragraph (1) may involve related agencies.
In addition to being implemented by Regional Apparatus and related agencies as referred to in paragraph (3), prevention (4) is also implemented by:
a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. community, NGOs, universities, community organizations, social organizations and religious organizations; and c. business sector.
