d. conduct examinations of evidence, records, or other documents concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children;
e. conduct examinations at certain places suspected of containing evidence;
f. conduct seizure of goods and materials resulting from violations that can be used as evidence in criminal cases related to violence against women and children;
g. request assistance from experts in the framework of carrying out investigation duties concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children; and
h. terminate the investigation if there is insufficient evidence of criminal acts related to violence against women and children.
In carrying out their authority, Civil Servant Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) shall coordinate with the National Police in accordance with the provisions (3) of laws and regulations.
(4) Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) shall notify the commencement of the investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the Public Prosecutor through the Investigation Official of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Code.

Article 41, Regional Governments may partner with the business sector, NGOs/social organizations concerned with women and children in the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
The partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out through: (2)
a. provision of information on employment opportunities for women victims of acts of violence;
b. education and training for women and children victims of acts of violence;
c. educational assistance for women and children victims of acts of violence who have been withdrawn from their education; d. fostering and increasing the economic independence of women victims of acts of violence;
e. providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities, private parties and various non-governmental organizations concerned with women and children from various forms of violence; and/or
g. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from various forms of violence up to the Village level.
The partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be set forth in the form of an agreement in accordance with (3) the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 28
Assistance services as referred to in Article 26 paragraph (1) letter number include: a. accompanying victims during the examination and health recovery process;
b. accompanying victims during the examination process at the police, prosecutor's office and court;
c. monitoring the interests and rights of victims in the examination process at the police, prosecutor's office and court; d. maintaining the privacy and confidentiality of victims from all parties who have no interest, including reporting by mass media;
e. coordinating with other assistants; and providing continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage.

